<div data-pf-editor-version="legacy" class="sc-jeyqhx jfeuyL __pf __pf_a6JLl64V" id="__pf"><div data-pf-type="Body" class="sc-djTQOc ejtSSi pf-7_"><div data-pf-type="Layout" class="sc-fatbYi kUsjkM pf-8_"><div data-section-id="pf-44c8" data-pf-type="Section" class="sc-epRwmx cpmRjY pf-9_ pf-color-scheme-1"><div style="--cw:1170px" class="sc-djVWQC dKziBg"><div class="sc-tafSX ePbmtR pf-10_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:12;--c-lg:12"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-pKreJ bIaXH pf-11_"><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-cyRdfs qmQNK pf-12_ pf-heading-1-h3"><span style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">MEN'S HEALTH INSIDER</span></h3></div></div></div></div></div><div data-section-id="pf-9fae" data-pf-type="Section" class="sc-epRwmx cpmRjY pf-14_ pf-color-scheme-1"><div style="--cw:1170px" class="sc-djVWQC dKziBg"><div class="sc-tafSX ePbmtR pf-15_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:8;--c-md:9;--c-lg:9"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-pKreJ bIaXH pf-16_"><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-cyRdfs qmQNK pf-17_ pf-heading-1-h3">Men Over 35 Are Losing Bedroom Confidence — And Doctors Are Blaming the Wrong Thing</h3><p class="sc-kUdmUV iejJTZ pf-19_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">Jan 01 2026 at 9:17 am EDT</p><p class="sc-kUdmUV iejJTZ pf-21_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">"It wasn't my age. It wasn't stress. It was something no one told me I'd lost — and one conversation with a friend changed everything."</p><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSBE8_adv.png?v=1771683378" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSBE8_adv.png?v=1771683378 1536w, https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSBE8_adv_500x.png?v=1771683378 320w" width="1920" height="1080" alt="HMX_NTV_MSBE8_adv.png__PID:56a1a9b3-ca97-4beb-b708-0a4917067e9e" data-action="url" data-href="/products/purrify" data-target="_self" data-pf-type="Image3" class="sc-gplwNw cwEcYX pf-23_ pf-image-1"/><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-cyRdfs qmQNK pf-24_ pf-heading-1-h3">My body quit on me.</h3><p class="sc-kUdmUV iejJTZ pf-26_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">If your body works fine on its own but shuts down the moment it matters...<br>
<br>&nbsp;If you've been blaming stress, age, or "being in your head"...<br><br>If you've tried pills, supplements, or lifestyle changes and <strong>nothing sticks...<br></strong><br>Then what I'm about to share might be the most important thing you read this year.<br><br>Because there's a hidden problem affecting <strong>millions of men over 35</strong>.<br><br>And the thing most doctors tell you to fix? It's not even the real cause.</p><img alt="HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png__PID:5a5079a6-714b-44ea-a110-538982d73839" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=2048" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=375 375w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=550 550w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=768 768w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=1024 1024w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=1280 1280w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=1440 1440w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=1680 1680w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=1800 1800w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=1920 1920w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_WCM1_adv.png?v=1771683840&width=2048 2048w" fetchPriority="low" decoding="async" loading="lazy" style="--pf-image-ratio:1.7777777777777777" width="1920" height="1080" sizes="75vw" data-action="url" data-href="/products/purrify" data-target="_self" data-pf-type="Image4" class="sc-lmUbDS jhRUAf pf-28_ pf-image-1" store="[object Object]"/><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-cyRdfs qmQNK pf-29_ pf-heading-1-h3">How I Almost Lost My Marriage Over Something I Couldn't Talk About</h3><p class="sc-kUdmUV iejJTZ pf-31_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">My name is William. I'm 44. Married. Two kids. Healthy by every standard my doctor could measure.<br><br>But for over a year, my body refused to do the one thing I couldn't ask for help with.<br><br>It started small. One bad night. Then two. Then it became a pattern.<br><br><strong>I'd get into bed with my wife and my body would just... shut off</strong>. Like a switch being flipped. No warning. No reason I could point to.<br><br>The worst part? It worked fine when I was alone.<br><br>Every. Single. Time.<br><br>But the moment she was there — the moment it actually mattered — something inside me went cold.<br><br>I told myself it was stress. The job. The kids. Being tired.<br><br>So I started going to bed earlier. Cut back on drinking. Hit the gym three times a week.<br><br><strong>Nothing changed.</strong></p><img alt="HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png__PID:a0760c53-3c4d-4786-a1a2-ac6747c56bf0" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=2048" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=375 375w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=550 550w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=768 768w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=1024 1024w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=1280 1280w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=1440 1440w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=1680 1680w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=1800 1800w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=1920 1920w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MWD1_adv.png?v=1771684079&width=2048 2048w" fetchPriority="low" decoding="async" loading="lazy" style="--pf-image-ratio:1.7777777777777777" width="1920" height="1080" sizes="75vw" data-action="url" data-href="/products/purrify" data-target="_self" data-pf-type="Image4" class="sc-lmUbDS jhRUAf pf-33_ pf-image-1" store="[object Object]"/><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-cyRdfs qmQNK pf-34_ pf-heading-1-h3">The $400 Doctor Visit That Told Me Nothing</h3><div class="sc-tafSX ePbmtR pf-36_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:12;--c-lg:12"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-pKreJ bIaXH pf-37_"><p class="sc-kUdmUV iejJTZ pf-38_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">I finally saw my doctor. He ran bloodwork. Testosterone? "Normal range." Heart? Fine. Thyroid? Fine.<br><br>He looked at me and said: <strong>"It's probably performance anxiety. Try to relax."</strong><br><br>Four hundred dollars to be told to relax.<br><br>I tried Viagra once. Ordered it online. It showed up in a plain brown box like something I should be ashamed of.<br><br>It worked on my body. But it didn't touch the real problem — <strong>the voice in my head</strong> that monitored everything. Am I still hard? Is it working? Can she tell?<br><br>I was medicated and still broken.<br><br><strong>I stopped initiating. Started avoiding her. Made excuses to stay up late so she'd be asleep when I came to bed.<br></strong><br>Our marriage was dying — and I couldn't tell a single person why.</p><img alt="HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png__PID:41a81de0-621e-49df-bf11-c9d663ef461a" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=2048" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=375 375w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=550 550w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=768 768w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=1024 1024w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=1280 1280w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=1440 1440w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=1680 1680w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=1800 1800w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=1920 1920w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MSIWN1_adv.png?v=1771684898&width=2048 2048w" fetchPriority="low" decoding="async" loading="lazy" style="--pf-image-ratio:1.7777777777777777" width="1920" height="1080" sizes="75vw" data-action="url" data-pf-type="Image4" class="sc-lmUbDS jhRUAf pf-40_ pf-image-1" store="[object Object]"/><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-cyRdfs qmQNK pf-41_ pf-heading-1-h3">The Conversation That Changed Everything</h3><p class="sc-kUdmUV iejJTZ pf-43_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">I was at my buddy Rick's place. Just the two of us. Late. And I let something slip I'd never said out loud.<br><br>Rick didn't laugh. He didn't flinch.<br><br>He said: <strong>"It's not in your head, man. It's your nervous system."</strong><br><br>He told me the male body has two modes. A survival mode — cortisol, fight or flight, high alert. And a performance mode — rest, connection, arousal.<br><br><strong>You can only perform in the second mode.<br></strong><br>And modern life — the screens, the stress, the constant low-level pressure — has locked most men's nervous systems in survival mode. Not enough to feel like a full panic attack. Just enough to shut down the one function your body thinks it doesn't need when it's under threat.<br><br>That's why it worked alone. Low threat, low cortisol.<br><br>That's why it died with her. Pressure arrives, cortisol spikes, and <strong>your body shuts down arousal to protect itself</strong>.<br><br>It's not weakness. It's not age. It's biology doing exactly what it's designed to do — for a man who's stuck in a mode he was never supposed to stay in.</p><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-cyRdfs qmQNK pf-45_ pf-heading-1-h3">Why Pills Will Never Fix This</h3><p class="sc-kUdmUV iejJTZ pf-47_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">Here's what Rick explained next — and this part made everything click.<br><br><strong>Pills force blood flow</strong>. That's all they do. They don't touch the nervous system. They don't address the cortisol lock. They don't stop the voice in your head.<br><br>That's why men take Viagra and still feel broken. The body cooperates, but the mind doesn't. Because the root problem was never blood flow. <strong>It was a nervous system stuck in survival mode</strong>.<br><br>For 200,000 years, men had a natural reset for this. Bare feet on the earth. Sleeping on the ground. Constant contact with the planet's magnetic field. That field kept the nervous system calibrated — pulling cortisol down and allowing the body to rest, recover, and perform.<br><br>Modern life severed that connection. Rubber shoes. Concrete floors. Screens. Wi-Fi. We removed the reset — and <strong>no one even noticed</strong>.</p><img alt="HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png__PID:af84cf7f-0dbf-41b9-b8f6-dff2c6ffc7ec" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=2048" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=375 375w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=550 550w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=768 768w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=1024 1024w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=1280 1280w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=1440 1440w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=1680 1680w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=1800 1800w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=1920 1920w,https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0632/7690/8587/files/HMX_NTV_MA1_adv.png?v=1771684205&width=2048 2048w" fetchPriority="low" decoding="async" loading="lazy" style="--pf-image-ratio:1.7777777777777777" width="1920" height="1080" sizes="75vw" data-pf-type="Image4" class="sc-lmUbDS jhRUAf pf-49_ pf-image-1" store="[object Object]"/><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-cyRdfs qmQNK pf-50_ pf-heading-1-h3">The Simple Thing Rick Showed Me</h3><p class="sc-kUdmUV iejJTZ pf-52_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">Rick rolled up his sleeve. A dark, heavy bracelet on his wrist.<br><br><strong>"Hematite,"</strong> he said. "Most iron-dense stone on earth. It generates a continuous magnetic field directly through skin contact. Same thing the ground used to do — except it works 24/7."<br><br>He'd been wearing it for five months. His wife had told mine he was "like a different man."<br><br>It was called <strong>Hemax</strong>. Not a cheap bead bracelet. <strong>30 grams of solid, premium-grade hematite</strong>. He said just wear it for a week.<br><br>I thought he was crazy. But I was desperate enough to try.</p><img alt="HMX_NTV_WHWM1_adv.png__PID:0e2bcda7-785f-4af4-8cc6-c6fb6e37639c" sr